Redis Set for Unique Registered Users
Write a Python program using a Redis Set to maintain unique registered user IDs. 
Add:

U101 U102 U103 U101 U104

Then:

Display all unique users. 
Check whether U102 exists. 
Remove U103.
Display the final set.


1.Add registered users

users = ["U101", "U102", "U103", "U101", "U104"]

for user in users: r.sadd("registered_users", user)

print("Users added successfully")
print("Unique users:", r.smembers("registered_users"))

2.Check whether U102 exists

if r.sismember("registered_users", "U102"): print("U102 exists")
else:
print("U102 does not exist")

3.Remove U103

r.srem("registered_users", "U103") 
print("U103 removed")
print("Final set:", r.smembers("registered_users"))
